pinctrl: sunxi: h713: PF6 as a GPIO

The H713 pin table knew bank F only up to PF5. PF6 exists: it is the
HY300PRO-G-EU's panel supply (stock panel_power_en), which U-Boot drives
at boot in h713_disp_stock_panel_power and the display MIPS driver now
cycles after a restart. Without the pin in the table a gpiod request for
it fails its pin-range lookup with -EPROBE_DEFER for good, and the
consumer never probes (seen 10.10.2026: the whole MIPS driver unbound).

Only the GPIO functions: nothing else is known about this pin. Built into
the kernel of the HY300PRO-G-EU test image, the panel cycle requested PF6
and brought the picture back after three restarts in a row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713.c
@@ -490,6 +490,13 @@
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x3, "mmc0"),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x4, "jtag"),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION_IRQ_BANK(0xe, 4, 5)),
+	/*
+	 * PF6: a GPIO the HY300PRO-G-EU uses as its panel supply (stock
+	 * panel_power_en, U-Boot's h713_disp_stock_panel_power); only its GPIO functions.
+	 */
+	SUNXI_PIN(SUNXI_PINCTRL_PIN(F, 6),
+		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x0, "gpio_in"),
+		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x1, "gpio_out")),
 	SUNXI_PIN(SUNXI_PINCTRL_PIN(G, 0),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x0, "gpio_in"),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x1, "gpio_out"),
